  "decision": "exclude",
  "confidence": 1.0,
  "reason": "The study uses in vitro methods (recombinant protein misfolding cyclic amplification) to investigate prion transmission barriers between species. It does not report any quantitative measure of agreement between non-human animal results and human clinical results, nor does it compare effect sizes. The focus is on in vitro prediction of amino acid sequences related to transmission barriers, not on comparing actual experimental outcomes in animals to human clinical outcomes."
